\end{align*}

The second equality follows from the fact that there are $3+n$ gloves in the box, $3$ of which are blue. Thus, $\prob{B_{1}} = \frac{3}{3 + n}$, and if we know that one blue glove has been removed from the box, where are now $2 + n$ total gloves in the box, $2$ of which are blue, so that, $\prob{BB | B_{1}} = \frac{2}{2 + n}$.

