\end{align*}

Since the support of each $X_i$ doesn't dependent on $\theta$, we will ignore the indicators and just consider the function. The likelihood function and log-likelihood function, respectively, are given by

\begin{align*}
    L(\theta) &= \displaystyle \prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i \mid \theta) = \prod_{i=1}^n \theta e^{-\theta x_i} = \theta^n e^{-\theta \sum x_i} \\
    l(\theta) &= \log(L(\theta)) = \log\left(\theta^n e^{-\theta \sum x_i}\right) = n\log(\theta) - \theta \sum x_i
\end{align*}

We can take the partial derivative of $l(\theta)$ to solve for the MLE. This yields $$\partial l/\partial \theta = \frac{n}{\theta} - \sum x_i = 0
