Therefore, $\hat{\theta}_{MLE} = \dfrac{n}{\sum X_i}$. Intuitively, this makes sense: The mean of the exponential distribution is $1/\lambda$, so as $\lambda$ represents an average rate of occurrence per unit time, we just take the reciprocal of the MLE for the mean time between occurrences. the MLE With the specified data, the answer is $1/3$.

The Normal distribution has two parameters, but we are assuming $\mu$ is known, so there is really only one unknown parameter here. The PDF of a $N(\mu,\sigma^2)$ distribution is 
\begin{align*}
